+# Adopted attempt recovery implementation
+
+Authority: `docs/design/adopted-attempt-predecessor-recovery.md` and the injected task.
+
+Follow the design handoff in order, without worktrees. Existing oversized modules
+receive the explicitly allowed narrow hooks and extractions; new modules stay
+within the design budgets. No runtime/workflow/provider changes.
+
+1. Implement byte overlay, materialization and broad-evidence hooks and overlay tests.
+2. Review overlay contract, then code quality.
+3. Implement and test committed predecessor lineage.
+4. Extract v1 structure helpers and add schema dispatch, lazy wrappers and CLI.
+5. Verify v1 unchanged and review.
+6. Implement logical views, incident, root-bound fixture and incident tests.
+7. Implement disposition v2, capture, exports and v2 tests.
+8. Run every Exact commands verification, including full non-e2e suite and CLI smoke.
+9. Obtain independent specification and code-quality reviews; address findings.
+10. Write result bundle with commits, command results and any work left undone.
+
+Affected surfaces: retirement source_bindings, materialization, broad_evidence,
+attempt_migration, package lazy exports, five new private modules, four new test
+modules and one fixture helper. Shared v1 archive/apply mechanics retain their
+validation, no-follow reads, exact replay and committed-review gates.
+
+Tradeoffs: future validator filesystem reads must use scope-aware primitives;
+later committed generation slots in the archived lineage directory invalidate
+that lineage; generation 5/11 remain fixed by the existing contract.
+
+Progress and command evidence are recorded in the task result bundle.
+
+## Recorded contract adjustment
+
+The design's unconditional HEAD lookup for every read scope conflicts with the
+required unchanged v1 behavior: the existing ledger builder passes a plan-only
+overlay while validating non-Git directories. The unchanged tests
+`test_materialization_retains_prior_generation` and
+`test_ledger_materializer_rejects_forged_plan_title` reproduced this conflict.
+Non-fallback scopes therefore permit an unavailable HEAD; opening or upgrading
+to committed fallback still requires a real HEAD. No file-fallback check is
+relaxed. The result bundle records this nearest compatible implementation.
+
+The scoped immutable-review listing also retains the existing closed-layout
+checks for malformed directories and symlinks. Enumerating only regular files,
+as sketched in the design, hid an invalid empty history directory when a caller
+supplied an unrelated overlay. Preserving v1 rejection takes precedence over
+that enumeration shortcut; uncommitted regular fallback files remain invisible.
+
+## Verification contract conflict
+
+The existing unmodified test
+`test_retirement_public_surface_is_cold_lazy_and_cli_sets_are_exact` in
+`tests/test_retirement_broad_evidence.py:5624` requires exactly the old 32 public
+exports. The task simultaneously requires two additional exports and prohibits
+modifying this test module. Both requirements cannot pass together. Preserve the
+required 34-name public API and leave the existing test unchanged; report its
+failure explicitly in `left_undone`, rather than weakening the assertion or
+making exports depend on the caller. All prescribed verification still runs.
+
+## Final review corrections
+
+Capture rejects absent outputs that Git would never report as individual
+untracked files (ignored paths, Git metadata paths, and paths below gitlinks).
+It also rejects ancestor/descendant collisions between outputs and migration
+roots before publication. These capture-only checks close cases where the
+design's initial output classifier could publish an incident and then fail
+publication or exact replay. Regression cases exercise the public capture API;
+the v1 path remains unchanged.
